      "role": "user",
      "content": "ok so here's what i got from yesterday. i had that interview at 10am at the tech firm downtown. i passed 4th and pike at around 9:42am. \n\n9:42:05 - Green light stayed on for 45 seconds (usually it's 30)\n9:43:10 - Red light felt much longer, like 90 seconds\n9:44:00 - Green light was super short, maybe 15 seconds\n\nthen later that afternoon i was meeting a new friend for coffee at 2pm. passed the same spot at 1:50pm.\n\n1:50:12 - Green light was exactly 30 seconds\n1:50:42 - Red light was 45 seconds\n1:51:27 - Green light was almost instant, maybe 10 seconds\n\nit feels like the long green at 9:42 was a 'go' for the interview, but the short green at 1:50 was a 'no' or a warning. does that timing sequence look like it means anything to you?",
